4.0.0 (unreleased):
    * BC PHP 8.2 minimum (PHP 8.1 dropped); Symfony 7 and 8 supported (Symfony 6 dropped)
    * BC Remove the Services container, ContainerInterface and the pimple/pimple suggestion: wiring belongs to the integration (ting_bundle)
    * BC Rename master/slave to primary/replica: ConnectionPool(Interface)::primary() / replica(), Connection::primary() / replica(), QueryInterface::selectPrimary() (now declared by the interface), Repository::pingPrimary(), $forcePrimary parameters, "primary" / "replicas" configuration keys; the names deprecated in 3.14 are removed, the old keys throw a ConfigException
    * BC Native types on the methods and properties of every interface and non-final class, SerializeInterface / UnserializeInterface included (mixed), and PHPDoc generics (Repository<T>, CollectionInterface<T>...): implementations and overrides written for 3.x, repositories included, must declare the 4.0 types (see UPGRADE-4.0.md)
    * BC Remove the constructors from ConnectionPoolInterface, StatementInterface and QueryInterface, and the unused SerializerFactoryInterface argument from RepositoryFactory::__construct() (Repository::__construct() lost it in 4.0.0-rc.1)
    * BC Replace the abandoned doctrine/cache with Symfony Cache Contracts: caches are Symfony\Contracts\Cache\CacheInterface pools, Ting\Cache\Cache only exposes get() and delete() (ConfigException before setCache()); Cached\Query::setVersion(), which had no effect, is removed; a negative TTL throws a QueryException
    * BC Repository reads (get(), getBy(), getOneBy()) take property names in the criteria, composite keys and order, and entity values converted by the serializer of the field (new Serializer\ArrayValueInterface and ScalarValueInterface); what 3.15 deprecated or sent as invalid SQL throws a ValueException (column names, empty criteria or IN list, bad order direction...)
    * BC Mutable fields modified in place are saved (new field option "mutable", on by default for Serializer\DateTime, Serializer\Json decoding objects and custom serializers): the unit of work keeps their database value and writes them when it differs, once their value is known (a partial read never overwrites them); isPropertyChanged() follows (see UPGRADE-4.0.md)
    * BC Saving an entity not managed whose autoincrement property holds an id (a clone, a detached entity, one restored from a cache or a session) updates its row by that id instead of inserting a new row; set the id to null to duplicate a row (see UPGRADE-4.0.md)
    * BC Unit of work lifecycle: a new entity is managed only once its INSERT has run (isManaged() is false before, and a failed INSERT can be saved again), manage() and NotifyProperty::addPropertyListener() add a listener once, and the changes made to an entity not managed (new, or detached) are no longer recorded
    * BC Two repositories mapping the same entity class: Repository::save() and delete() write with the metadata of the repository, and the unit of work tracks each entity with the metadata that read it, instead of those of the last repository built (UnitOfWork::manage(), pushSave() and pushDelete() take a new optional metadata parameter)
    * BC Several metadata mapping a table: the hydrator chooses by the database and schema of the result (or objectDatabaseIs() / objectSchemaIs()), then by the repository running the query (new Hydrator::preferRepository()), and throws a HydratorException naming the candidates when they stay ambiguous, instead of taking the first or the last registered
    * BC A hydrator with identity map starts a new one for each result (kept as a service, it returned entities of an earlier result, or stale ones after reset() / detach()); the protected Hydrator::$alreadyManaged is removed, and a subclass overriding getIterator() must read its rows through hydratedRows() (see docs/hydrators.md)
    * BC HydratorRelational throws a HydratorException when its relations form a cycle, when an alias of a relation is not in the result, or when the entity of an alias lacks a primary key value (its entities were merged under one key), instead of ignoring them or merging silently; rows without root entity are skipped
    * BC Serializers: DateTimeImmutable writes Y-m-d H:i:s by default instead of ATOM; DateTime / DateTimeImmutable only read the formats databases return (no PHP date parser fallback), and a format without time reads midnight; Json honours JSON_OBJECT_AS_ARRAY and JSON_PARTIAL_OUTPUT_ON_ERROR, its errors always throw a RuntimeException; int-backed BackedEnum and Ip reject a value that is not an integer
    * BC PostgreSQL rows are keyed as PostgreSQL names the columns: an expression without alias is named by a minimal rule, a column aliased without AS goes to the entity of its table, identifiers follow PostgreSQL case folding (with a case-insensitive fallback, MySQL too), a multi-statement query is read from its last statement, and a column count mismatch throws a QueryException (see UPGRADE-4.0.md)
    * BC PostgreSQL bool fields without serializer: 'f' is read as false, and the Pgsql driver sends a PHP boolean as '1' / '0' (false was sent as '', which PostgreSQL rejects for a boolean)
    * BC Query parameters: a missing parameter throws a QueryException with every driver (PostgreSQL and Mysqli prepared queries sent NULL); Mysqli non-prepared queries send an escaped colon (\:) as ":", as the other drivers; Mysqli / Pgsql escapeField() escape a colon in a column name; SphinxQL sends null as NULL and booleans as 0 / 1
    * BC Driver failures are reported: Mysqli / Pgsql setTimezone() throws a DriverException when the server rejects the value (an invalid "timezone" option, ignored by 3.x, now fails every query on that database); a charset rejected when reconnect() / ping() re-apply it is no longer kept as current (Pgsql reconnect() returned false), and Mysqli setCharset() throws a DriverException instead of a mysqli_sql_exception under MYSQLI_REPORT_STRICT
    * BC Transactions: startTransaction(), commit() and rollback() throw a TransactionException when the database refuses them, and commit() throws when the connection was lost during the transaction
    * BC Prepared queries follow their connection: PreparedQuery and Cached\PreparedQuery prepare their statement again when the target connection changes (a write after a read ran on the replica, selectPrimary(true) was ignored) or when its session is gone after a reconnection (new StatementInterface::isStale())
    * BC Util\Debug::export(), broken by typed properties in 4.0.0-rc.1, exports objects as arrays with a __CLASS__ key, dates with their value, the private properties of parent classes and iterables with object keys (WeakMap), without consuming generators nor recursing forever on a negative depth
    * BC NotifyProperty::__serialize() and __debugInfo() return mangled keys (the private properties of a parent or child class were silently lost in a cache or a session) and __serialize() honours __sleep() (ignored since 3.12); payloads written by 3.x are still read, and 3.13 reads those written by 4.0
    * BC ResultInterface::setObjectToFetch(), added in 4.0.0-rc.1, is removed: HydratorValueObject builds its objects from the rows, with or without cache (a cache hit returned raw rows), and no longer writes a static property named after a column
    * Include the 3.13.0 to 3.15.0 changes: ResetInterface on ConnectionPool, UnitOfWork and Repository (worker mode); the 3.14 / 3.15 deprecations are removed as listed above
    * Add Connection::getName() and optional driver interfaces, implemented by the Pgsql driver: SequenceAwareDriverInterface (getInsertedIdForSequence()), DefaultValuesInsertDriverInterface (an entity without value is inserted with INSERT INTO t DEFAULT VALUES: PostgreSQL rejected () VALUES ()) and RollbackListenerAwareDriverInterface (Mysqli too, see the retry fix below)
    * Tooling: tests migrated from atoum to PHPUnit; PHPStan level 8 without baseline, with a type coverage check
    * Fix regressions of 4.0.0-rc.1 in the drivers: Mysqli prepared queries bind their parameters again (NULL was bound, ccmbenchmark/ting#108) and return true without result set; Mysqli Driver::execute() without collection and Query::query() on a statement without result set no longer throw a TypeError; drivers work again without ConnectionPool and without user or password
    * Fix other regressions of 4.0.0-rc.1: collections and hydrators are Countable again; Hydrator::objectSchemaIs() overrides the schema read by Pgsql again; Pgsql reads a column without table again and logs the query with its named parameters; Serializer\BackedEnum::serialize() returns a string again; a cached collection without result comes back empty
    * Fix the unit of work after a failure (since 3.x): a failed process() no longer replays its query on the next save; an entity whose generated id cannot be written back is not inserted twice, one inserted in a rolled back transaction is inserted again; a change made by the setter of the id is saved; a nested process() writes nothing twice (see docs/unit-of-work.md)
    * Fix the unit of work bookkeeping (since 3.x): changing a primary key targets the old value (it sent WHERE key IN (old, new)), and primary keys are read through their custom getter and serialized in the WHERE clause; a saved entity without change is unqueued; detach() raises no warning; pushDelete() of an entity never inserted runs no query; a change of a property not mapped is ignored
    * Fix Util\PropertyAccessor (since 3.x): it writes a private property of a parent class, a readonly, private(set) or protected(set) property and a PHP 8.4 virtual property instead of throwing; an INSERT skips a typed property not initialized unless its custom getter handles it; a PSR cache hit is kept in memory (new key prefix write_property_v2_)
    * Fix hydrators (since 3.x): HydratorRelational no longer depends on the order of its relations nor drops one sharing a source alias; the identity map tells composite keys apart; objectDatabaseIs() applies to its alias only; a reused hydrator forgets the metadata of its aliases; mapObjectTo() / mapAliasTo() skip an alias whose entity is null (LEFT JOIN)
    * Fix HydratorAggregator (since 3.x): the last group is no longer dropped when the rows are not sorted, a group identifier neither int nor string (Uuid, array) is supported, and a null identifier (every row was lost) or one that cannot be serialized throws a HydratorException
    * Fix objects used without a result or before their configuration: collections and hydrators without result iterate as empty, first() / count() no longer disturb a running foreach, Query, Metadata, hydrators and Pgsql Statement / Result throw a Ting exception instead of a TypeError or an Error; findMetadataForEntity() on an unknown entity does nothing, SphinxQL escapeField() without field returns ''
    * Fix MetadataRepository registering an entity '' for a metadata without entity (PHP 8.5 deprecation), and Metadata::getRepository() returning null for metadata loaded by batchLoadMetadata() / batchLoadMetadataFromCache() (since 3.x)
    * Fix the generated queries (since 3.x): the columns of the WHERE clause of get() / getBy() / getOneBy() are escaped (reserved words, mixed case); parameters are named after their role and position (v1_name, w1_id, w2_id__1), so that any column name works and an IN list no longer collides with another column; getByCriteria() no longer emits an empty ORDER BY
    * Fix connections sharing a driver (since 3.x): ConnectionPool keys the drivers without collision; Mysqli prepared statements are cached per database, and their results labeled with the connection running them; the Pgsql connection string quotes every value (an empty password, spaces, quotes) and errors redact the user and password
    * Fix reconnections (since 3.x): Pgsql reconnect() opens a new session; Mysqli ping() retries after a failed reconnection; reconnect() before connect() throws a NeverConnectedException; a failing mysqli_init() throws a DriverException; charset and timezone are applied to every new session; a Pgsql statement destructor no longer throws on a closed connection
    * Fix Pgsql prepared statements (since 3.x): one failing in a transaction is deallocated once the transaction ends (a retry failed with "prepared statement ... already exists"), and getAffectedRows() reports the last query, prepared or not
    * Fix driver errors and the query log (since 3.x): Pgsql failures no longer raise a PHP warning before Ting's exception (an ErrorException under Symfony debug); the query log is stopped when a query, a prepare or an execution fails; a parameter parsing failure (PCRE limit) throws a QueryException; Mysqli prepared queries without parameter no longer throw a ValueError
    * Fix floats sent with 14 significant digits (since 3.x, the precision ini setting): they are sent with the digits that read back as the same float, with a '.' whatever the locale; Pgsql sends INF / NAN as Infinity / NaN, Mysqli throws a QueryException for them in a query that is not prepared
    * Fix the PostgreSQL column parser (since 3.x) on valid queries whose columns were lost, shifted or hydrated into the wrong entity: COUNT(*), DISTINCT, ARRAY[...], literals, quoted identifiers, comments, dollar quotes, keywords as aliases, parenthesized SELECTs, UNION, WITH, FROM lists, sub-queries, derived tables, CTEs; long queries no longer hit the PCRE limit (tables lost silently)
    * Security: Mysqli Driver::execute() quotes string values with single quotes; double quotes allowed SQL injection under the sql_mode NO_BACKSLASH_ESCAPES (real_escape_string() then only doubles single quotes) and made values identifiers under ANSI_QUOTES

    Developer experience:
    * Typed query parameters: setParams() of every query sends a DateTimeInterface as Y-m-d H:i:s, a BackedEnum as its value, and expands an array into an IN list (:ids becomes :ids__1, :ids__2...); an empty list, a null or nested element, a pure enum or an object neither Stringable nor convertible throw a QueryException (see docs/queries.md)
    * Repository::getBySql() / getOneBySql() read the entities of the repository with a query of your own (prepared), without building a HydratorSingleObject collection
    * Repository::transactional(callable) commits when the callback returns, rolls back and throws again when it throws
    * Repository::countBy(), existsBy() and deleteBy() count, test and delete by criteria, with the rules of getBy()
    * getBy() takes an offset (pagination), getOneBy() an order
    * Query::queryValue() returns the first column of the first row (COUNT(*), MAX()...), CollectionInterface::toArray() the items in a list
    * Repository::getQueryBuilder() is typed by its $type (PHPDoc): no more @var on the Aura builder
    * A "datetime" field without serializer hydrates a DateTimeImmutable when its property is typed DateTimeImmutable, nullable or not (same Y-m-d H:i:s format, immutable field); a property typed DateTimeInterface, DateTime or a union, or not typed, still gets a DateTime, as in 3.x (a DateTimeInterface property can hold a DateTime)

4.0.0-rc.1 (2025-12-15):
    * BC PHP 8.0 dropped, minimum version is now PHP 8.1
    * BC All classes now fully typehinted with strict types and return types
    * BC Pgsql Driver now uses native PHP 8.1+ PgSql\Connection and PgSql\Result classes instead of resources
    * Serializers typehinted (SerializeInterface and UnserializeInterface keep their 3.x signatures: the native return types were removed before this release)
    * BC Added ping() and setTimezone() methods to DriverInterface
    * BC Added ConnectionPoolInterface::setDatabaseOptions() method
    * BC Deleted Metadata::getGetter() and Metadata::getSetter() methods
    * BC Deleted deprecated getInsertId() methods on Mysqli and Pgsql drivers (use getInsertedId() instead)
    * BC Deleted deprecated getInsertIdForSequence() on Pgsql driver (use getInsertedIdForSequence() instead)
    * BC Deleted deprecated getInsertId() on QueryInterface and Query class (use getInsertedId() instead)
    * BC Deleted Generator::getByCriteriaWithOrderAndLimit(), merged into Generator::getByCriteria() with $order and $limit parameters
    * BC Deleted UnitOfWork::generateUid() and UnitOfWork::generateUUID() methods
    * New feature: HydratorValueObject allows hydrating simple objects without metadata using native fetch_object() methods
    * New feature: ResultInterface::setObjectToFetch() for value object hydration (corrected entry: no fetchObject() method was ever exposed; setObjectToFetch() was removed in 4.0.0, see above)
    * Improvement: UnitOfWork now uses WeakMap exclusively for internal entity storage (enhanced from PHP 8.0 implementation)
    * Improvement: PHPStan analysis raised to level 7 with baseline significantly reduced (from ~2200 to <50 errors)
    * Improvement: Type coverage tool added (tomasvotruba/type-coverage) with minimum thresholds: 97% return types, 85% param types, 83% property types
    * Improvement: Rector configuration added for automated refactoring and code quality improvements (targeting PHP 8.0+)
    * Improvement: PHPStan custom extension for properties (CCMBenchmark\Ting\PHPStan\PropertiesExtension)
    * Security: prevent SQL injection in Pgsql Driver::getInsertedIdForSequence() (corrected entry: shipped in this release, listed in 4.0.0 before)

3.15.0 (2026-10-05):
    * Repository::get() (composite primary key), getBy() / getOneBy() criteria and the getBy() order now all take
      property names, converted to column names by the Metadata
    * Deprecate column names in these keys: a key that is not a property but is the column of a field still works
      and triggers a silenced E_USER_DEPRECATED. A key that is both a property and the column of another field is
      the property
    * Deprecate order directions other than ASC / DESC (case-insensitive): still ignored, they trigger a silenced
      E_USER_DEPRECATED and will throw a ValueException in 4.0. An order whose directions are all ignored no longer
      produces an invalid "ORDER BY" clause
    * Criteria values (getBy(), getOneBy() and get()) are converted by the serializer of their field:
        * an object is serialized (enum, DateTime, Uuid...); an object for a field without serializer throws a
          ValueException, except a Stringable object which is still sent as is
        * an array becomes an IN list of converted values, an empty array throws a ValueException
          (it produced an invalid "IN ()" before), check it first: if ($ids === []) { return ...; }
        * an array for a field whose serializer implements the new Serializer\ArrayValueInterface (Json does) is
          serialized as a whole and compared with "=". The result depends on the column type: a TEXT column matches
          when the encoding is the same, a MySQL JSON column compared to a string never matches, PostgreSQL has no
          "=" operator for json (jsonb has one)
        * null (IS NULL) and scalars are unchanged

3.14.0 (2026-10-05):
    * Security: prevent SQL injection in Pgsql Driver::getInsertedIdForSequence() (backport from 4.0.0-rc.1)
    * Drop Symfony 6 and PHP 8.1 support, PHP >= 8.2 is now required
    * Add Symfony 8 support
    * Tests: migrate from atoum to PHPUnit
    * Add primary/replica names: ConnectionPool::primary() / replica(), Connection::primary() / replica(),
      Query::selectPrimary() and Repository::pingPrimary()
    * Connection configuration now uses the "primary" and "replicas" keys
    * Deprecate ConnectionPool::master() / slave(), Connection::master() / slave(), Query::selectMaster()
      and Repository::pingMaster(): they trigger a silenced E_USER_DEPRECATED and delegate to the new methods
    * Deprecate the "master" and "slaves" connection configuration keys: they trigger a silenced E_USER_DEPRECATED
      and are converted to "primary" / "replicas" (the new key wins when both are given)
    * ConnectionPoolInterface::master() / slave() are deprecated, they will be replaced by primary() / replica() in 4.0.
      Connection uses primary() / replica() when the pool provides them, master() / slave() otherwise
    * Fix Cached\PreparedQuery: selectPrimary() (formerly selectMaster()) is now honoured for reading queries

